<title>JAPAN: Japan Mar industrial output down revised 0.3.</title>
<headline>Japan Mar industrial output down revised 0.3.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in March fell a revised 0.3 percent from the previous month, compared with a revised preliminary estimate of a 0.7 percent fall, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year comparison, industrial production in March rose a revised 7.6 percent, against a revised preliminary estimate of a 7.4 percent increase.</p>
<p>Industry output for fiscal 1996/97 rose a revised 4.0 percent from a preliminary 4.1 percent and the calendar 1996 figure was revised to a 2.7 percent increase.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			  MAR     PRELIM    MONTH AGO MARINDEX</p>
<p> Output		 -0.3    -0.7    -3.7    101.2</p>
<p> Shipments	    +0.8     0.0    -4.3    104.4</p>
<p> Inventories	  -2.7    -2.4    -0.7    103.3</p>
<p> Inventories-to-</p>
<p> -Shipments ratio   -3.5    -2.7     +0.8    106.2</p>
<p>Capacity utilisation</p>
<p>rate		    +0.7    N.A.    -3.7     89.4</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>			  MAR	   MONTH AGO</p>
<p>Output		  +7.6	   +3.1</p>
<p>Shipments	     +9.0	   +4.0</p>
<p>Inventories	   -5.5	   -3.3</p>
<p>Inventories-to-</p>
<p>-Shipments ratio    -11.2	  -4.9</p>
<p>Capacity utilisation</p>
<p>rate		    +6.1	   +1.7</p>
